like-for-like
Same shape: a pool of cell objects, each with its alive flag, next state and its own list of its eight neighbors' coordinates, linked in the reference's order; same two-pass generation; same seeding with the reference's random generator. The reference's checksum (live cells plus the FNV-1a hash of the flags) is computed after the timed generations in both. Stores are range-checked; state is unlogged, so nothing is saved for a rollback.
